{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00563",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.91,
      "end_seconds": 13.67,
      "duration_seconds": 12.76,
      "text": "Come in, do sit down. Before we begin, how would you like me to address you? Mr. Pemberton, or something more informal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.78,
      "end_seconds": 24.46,
      "duration_seconds": 9.68,
      "text": "Mr. Pemberton is perfectly fine, thank you. Though my friends call me Alistair, if you prefer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.54,
      "end_seconds": 32.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "Mr. Pemberton it is, for now. Tell me what has brought you in this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.56,
      "end_seconds": 53.75,
      "duration_seconds": 18.19,
      "text": "Well, I woke at about six and found my left arm and leg felt rather weak. Heavy, you might say. It was quite sudden, or rather, it was there as soon as I woke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.29,
      "end_seconds": 64.68,
      "duration_seconds": 9.39,
      "text": "So you woke up with weakness down your left side. Did you notice it before you went to bed?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.61,
      "end_seconds": 74.96,
      "duration_seconds": 9.35,
      "text": "I did not. I was perfectly well last night. I watched the news and went up at ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.86,
      "end_seconds": 80.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Understood. How long has it been there now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.38,
      "end_seconds": 97.31,
      "duration_seconds": 13.93,
      "text": "About three hours. It was worse when I first stood up. It has eased slightly since, but I would not say it has gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.3,
      "end_seconds": 112.4,
      "duration_seconds": 12.1,
      "text": "All right. So, weakness down the left side, there since you woke, and a little better but not gone. Have I got that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.52,
      "end_seconds": 115.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Exactly right, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.91,
      "end_seconds": 123.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "Good. Has anything made it better or worse that you've noticed?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.32,
      "end_seconds": 135.11,
      "duration_seconds": 9.79,
      "text": "Not that I can say. I tried shaking the arm out, but that did not seem to change anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.56,
      "end_seconds": 148.63,
      "duration_seconds": 11.07,
      "text": "Fair enough. Now I need to ask about your speech. Any problem with your speech, finding words or slurring?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.24,
      "end_seconds": 161.13,
      "duration_seconds": 9.89,
      "text": "No. My wife says I sound entirely like myself, which she does not always mean as a compliment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.37,
      "end_seconds": 178.4,
      "duration_seconds": 15.03,
      "text": "Ha. Then let me have a look at you. First, I'd like to look at your face. Could you smile for me, and show me your teeth?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.2,
      "end_seconds": 186.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.57,
      "end_seconds": 195.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "Lovely. Now raise your eyebrows, and close your eyes tightly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.43,
      "end_seconds": 200.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Certainly. Is this all right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.45,
      "end_seconds": 226.88,
      "duration_seconds": 16.43,
      "text": "Yes. Your face looks even on both sides. Now hold both arms out in front of you, palms up, and squeeze my fingers with each hand in turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.81,
      "end_seconds": 235.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "I do notice the left one is a little slower to come up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.92,
      "end_seconds": 247.6,
      "duration_seconds": 11.68,
      "text": "I can feel that you squeeze with both hands, and the strength in both arms is equal. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.48,
      "end_seconds": 253.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Does that mean it is nothing at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.31,
      "end_seconds": 273.69,
      "duration_seconds": 19.38,
      "text": "What I can tell you is what I found. Your face is even, your arms are equal in strength, and your speech is normal. I'm not going to give it a name today, because I'd be guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.58,
      "end_seconds": 282.3,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "I would rather you be honest than reassure me for the sake of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.3,
      "end_seconds": 305.33,
      "duration_seconds": 22.03,
      "text": "Then here's the honest part. We watch it carefully. If any of these happen, you must not wait and see: your face drops on one side, your speech goes slurred or muddled, or the weakness gets worse. In that case you call 999 immediately."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.96,
      "end_seconds": 313.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "Face, speech, weakness. I have seen the advertisement on television."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.73,
      "end_seconds": 327.36,
      "duration_seconds": 11.63,
      "text": "Exactly that one. And your wife should know it too, so she can act if you're not able to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.87,
      "end_seconds": 336.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "I shall tell her this evening. She will be rather pleased to have a job."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.04,
      "end_seconds": 344.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.88,
      "text": "Good. Rest today, don't drive, and keep your phone within reach."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.68,
      "end_seconds": 354.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "Not driving is no hardship. I am not very fond of the motorway anyway."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.45,
      "end_seconds": 371.58,
      "duration_seconds": 16.13,
      "text": "Then that is settled. Now, if it hasn't gone away within three days, I want you back here to see me, even if you feel it's improving."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.76,
      "end_seconds": 380.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.54,
      "text": "If it has not gone in three days, I return. Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.15,
      "end_seconds": 392.62,
      "duration_seconds": 10.47,
      "text": "Do ring the surgery in the morning to book that, so you're not waiting in a queue."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 394.91,
      "end_seconds": 401.44,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "I shall. Is there anything else I should do in the meantime?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.68,
      "end_seconds": 412.59,
      "duration_seconds": 9.91,
      "text": "Plenty of water, a light lunch, and gentle movement of the arm and leg. No heavy lifting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.94,
      "end_seconds": 416.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Gentle movement. Very good."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 419.25,
      "end_seconds": 426.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.77,
      "text": "Do you have any questions for me before you go, Mr. Pemberton?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 426.95,
      "end_seconds": 432.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Only whether I should telephone my sister. She worries terribly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 434.61,
      "end_seconds": 444.55,
      "duration_seconds": 9.94,
      "text": "Do ring her, and let her know the plan, so that someone else is aware of it too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 447.4,
      "end_seconds": 451.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I'm grateful for your time."
    }
  ]
}
